Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:52:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] lakeside r2 brightness: sun 0.5 -> 0.7 + warm
 hemisphere-ambient fill (zero lights, zero draw calls) + water refit

Grok Bot review: the v3.4 colour-space fix was right but the frame went dark and lost the r5h3 sunset warmth (backlit far
trees / roofs). No extra light (each light adds a pass to every batch), no material/vertex edits, fog untouched:
- sun 0.5 -> 0.7 of base; ambient 0.2 -> 0.49 of base with a warm hemisphere: sky 0.0107/0.0656/0.1106 (r5h3 zenith
  0.0116/0.2747/0.4793 dimmed, less blue), ground 1/0.841/0.0687 (r5h3 1/0.5457/0.1441 warmer) - up faces get the dim sky,
  camera-facing backlit faces about half warm ground.
- water-only scales refit under it: main 1.67 -> 1.37, ambient 1.27 -> 1.85, sky 0.8 -> 0.35, floor 0.30 -> 0.31
  (params + effect defaults lightParams/specParams).
- night illuminance ratios follow so night/day keeps moon/sun 0.857 and ambient 0.219 (lakeside-light-encoding):
  sun 0.617 -> 0.864, ambient 0.694 -> 1.76.
Mac-calibrated Blender G-buffer emulator, board camera, layered fog (r5h3 / emu, luma ratio): near water 66/152/146 / 59/153/146
0.99; bridge deck 104/128/116 / 121/141/117 1.11; grass_L 81/107/24 / 109/134/59 1.29; far trees 71/83/20 / 31/95/16 1.00;
roof 131/37/2 / 135/44/10 1.12. Grass stays ~+29% at any sun >= 0.7 and the far hills stay green (albedo) - see README.
Tests dirlight / water_fog follow.
